hey. 14:15; 17:29; Ps 115:4-8; 135:15-18; Isa 44:10-20; 46:5-8 Jer 10:3-5,11,14,15; Ho 8:6; 1Co 8:4; 10:19,20; 12:2; Ga 4:8 made. 35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-19-27","title":"Acts 19:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>that not. 21; Zep 2:11; Mt 23:14; 1Ti 6:5 whom. 1Jo 5:19; Re 13:3,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-19-28","title":"Acts 19:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>they. 7:54; 16:19-24; 21:28-31; Ps 2:2; Re 12:12 and cried. 34,35; 1Sa 5:3-5; 1Ki 18:26-29; Isa 41:5-7; Jer 50:38; Re 13:4 Re 17:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-19-29","title":"Acts 19:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>the whole. 32; 17:8; 21:30,38 Gaius. Ro 16:23; 1Co 1:14 Aristarchus. 20:4; 27:2; Col 4:10; Phm 1:24 Macedonia.Macedonia, an extensive province of Greece, was bounded on the north by the mountains of Haemus, on the south by Epirus and Achaia, on the east by the Aegean sea and Thrace, and on the west by the Adriatic sea; celebrated in all histories as being the third kingdom which, under Alexander the Great, obtained the empire of the world, and had under it 150 nations.</p>\n<p>the theatre. 1Co 4:9; *Gr:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-19-30","title":"Acts 19:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Paul. 14:14-18; 17:22-31; 21:39 the disciples. 2Sa 18:2,3; 21:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-19-31","title":"Acts 19:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>the chief. 10; 16:6; Pr 16:7 desiring. 21:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-19-32","title":"Acts 19:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chap